The lab was really Ari’s spare bedroom because the real lab had NDAs that creaked when you touched them. He’d built the two stacks in a piece of modular synthesis software that never asked what you believed; it just let you wire oscillators to filters and see if the world sang. On screen: two near-identical networks, a NAND ladder and a NOR ladder, both wrapped in a Gaussian kernel that looked like a friendly hat. A threshold 
